※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ One arm gives the arena back and the other gives `x` something new.  After the `if`, `x` is
※ dead along one of the two ways that reach the join, so it is dead: a name read later cannot
※ tell which way it came.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(s)
    let c: bool = true
    let x: mut str = "a" ⧺ "b" in s
    if c:
        ⎕empty(s)
    else:
        x ← "new"
    if x = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
